Transport is implementation-specific.

Could be:

HTTP
WebSocket
gRPC
message queue
decentralized protocols

MOS defines semantics, not transport.

18. Multi-Agent Coordination

Multiple nodes MAY cooperate through:

shared Intent
delegated Capabilities
negotiated Decisions
synchronized Knowledge

Example:

Research Agent

        │

        ▼

Market Analysis Intent

        │

 ┌──────┼──────┐

 ▼      ▼      ▼

News   SEC   Quant

Agent Agent Agent

        │

        ▼

Portfolio Decision
19. Communication Learning

MOS MAY learn:

which agents are reliable,
which communication paths are efficient,
which delegations succeed,
which messages are valuable.

Communication history becomes cognition.

20. Explainability

Every communication SHALL answer:

Who communicated?
Why?
Under which authority?
What information was exchanged?
What decisions followed?
What impact occurred?
21. Compliance

A MOS implementation complies with RFC-0008 if:

communication is represented cognitively,
nodes have identity,
messages preserve provenance,
delegation is explicit,
trust is modeled,
conflicts are preserved,
synchronization is explainable.
